<Base title="Benchmarks · XMR4EL">
  <h1>Benchmark — 2 November 2026</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    One configuration, two datasets, three comparators, and every caveat we could find.
  </p>
  <p>
    XMR4EL beats SapBERT 1-NN on NCBI-disease and trails it on BC5CDR-chemical. On ambiguous mention
    keys, those seen in training with more than one label, it does better on both. There is one trained
    tree per dataset and no repeated seeds, so treat this as evidence worth following up, not a final
    ranking.
  </p>
  <p class="muted">
    Source: <a href="https://github.com/lasigeBioTM/XMR4EL/blob/main/docs/BENCHMARK.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">XMR4EL benchmark report</a>.
    Recorded source commit: <code>aeca7a4</code>.
  </p>

