  <section id="ablation">
    <h2>4. Nearest-neighbour reweighting ablation</h2>
    <p>
      The script fixes an evaluation-only ablation on the same trees, turning off reweighting
      (beta 10 → 0). Recorded evaluation protocols, population and mention-group hashes, other search
      settings and candidate recall match the beta-10 evaluations. Net correct-count losses use
      full-precision accuracies and kept-row counts.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap" role="region" aria-labelledby="cap-abl" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <caption id="cap-abl">Acc@1 with beta 10 → beta 0</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Dataset</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">Dev</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">Test</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">Net correct rows lost, dev / test (derived)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">NCBI-disease</th>
            <td class="num">0.926 → 0.892</td><td class="num">0.895 → 0.771</td><td class="num">25 / 114</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">BC5CDR-chemical</th>
            <td class="num">0.946 → 0.603</td><td class="num">0.933 → 0.631</td><td class="num">1,776 / 1,559</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Candidate recall is unchanged. On BC5CDR-chemical dev, seen-1 accuracy drops from 0.977 to 0.636:
      36.4% of those rows are misranked without reweighting. The beta-zero scores still combine leaf
      matcher probabilities with ancestor routing-path probabilities.
    </p>
  </section>

